# Novel Factory layers

Before writing new code, state the layer. If it is Presentation, do not modify Core.

## DOMAIN

Novels, chapters, characters, models, memory, providers, workflow events as facts.

May enter Core (this package except `gui/`).

## APPLICATION

Generate / edit a chapter, load a book, assign a model, ping a provider, run a workflow.

May enter `FactoryService` / `Workflow` / pipeline. Return business DTOs (`BookStatus`, `ChapterResult`, `ProviderStatus`, `WorkflowEvent`).

## PRESENTATION

Dropdowns, cards, tabs, badges, steppers, dashboards, filters, display names (`Planning`, `Configured`, `Inherit Default`, `✓●○`).

Must stay in `gui/` (`presentation/`, pages, adapters). CLI copy belongs in `cli.print_progress`, not Core.

Forbidden in FactoryService, ModelRegistry, events.py, Agent, Workflow:

- `get_xxx_page()` / `get_xxx_board()` / `get_xxx_dropdown()`
- `ModelRegistry.xxx_options()`
- `WorkflowEvent.track_xxx` or stepper glyphs
- GUI-only DTO fields (`label` for widgets, card/panel/tab/badge types)

Exception: the concept is a real CLI + GUI + Web business fact, not a screen.

One Core, two interfaces. Deleting `gui/` must leave CLI/Core working.
